// tmpguard -- fail when building a tree leaves anything behind in /tmp.
//
//   tmpguard IDC_ROOT TREE...
//
// IDC_ROOT is the idc directory (the one holding bin/idc). Each TREE is built
// with the standard library, IDC_FRESH_CASES=TREE and a private TMPDIR, so every test case of the
// tree really runs (idstd's stay cached), and /tmp is listed before and after. Every entry
// the build added is named, and the exit status is 1 when any build failed or
// left an entry, 2 for a usage error, 0 otherwise. Other programs writing to
// /tmp while it runs show up as entries too, so run it on a quiet machine.
main(int argc, string[] argv) {
  int rc = tg_go(argc, argv, (import tg_watch));
} return int rc;
(1, ["tmpguard"]):(2) then eprints:("usage: tmpguard IDC_ROOT TREE...\n")
(2, ["tmpguard", "/r"]):(2) then eprints:("usage: tmpguard IDC_ROOT TREE...\n")
